{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Behold</b> — a small amount, like something measured by handbreadths." "<b>And my span</b> — like חדל, as כבש and כשב and שמלה and שלמה [i.e., root letters alternating with weak letters]." "<b>Surely every man is but vanity</b> — this is 'every man,' and the meaning is like: vanity of vanities." "<b>And the meaning of נצב</b> — it is so forever; it will not change, that he departs from the rank of vanity."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:15.543150980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}